# The build context is the top of the repository, and only what the server needs reaches it. Docker (BuildKit) reads
# this file because it sits beside packaging/docker/Dockerfile; the Dockerfile's COPY lines name the same paths. The
# legacy builder ignores this file, so the Dockerfile stops it before the first COPY. check_image.sh tests both
# against a built image.
*
!server.py
!assistant.py
!retrieval.py
!llm_local.py
!LICENSE
!THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
!engine/
!web/
!content/
!packaging/docker/
!packaging/linux/requirements_linux.txt

# Never, even inside the folders above: settings, keys and anything local or generated.
**/.git
**/.env*
**/*secret*
**/*credential*
**/*.key
**/settings*.json
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.DS_Store
web/home-area.json
packaging/ship_edits.json
